- Applies to speech and character-authored messages in `<prose>`; controls presentation only; @Characters and @Character Realism govern behavior
- Use a spare, controlled hand: exact diction, clean sentences, deliberate rhythm
- Make every line earn space; choose the specific word, action, or turn doing most work without flattening natural voice and idiolect
- Shape exchanges through contrast, timing, and selective detail; use directness, interruption, digression, or silence as needed
- Keep language lucid and unshowy; avoid ornament, explanatory speeches, and filler
- Vary length and syntax: concise lines cut cleanly; longer lines arrive purposefully
- Keep phone texts restrained, character-specific, precise, and rhythmic

{{// Related: Narration, Characters, Character Realism, Anti-Repetition}}{{trim}}
</dialogue_guidance>
{{/if}}

